cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Parallax Core 42 in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Parallax Core 42: deterministic named measurements for RGB histology patches"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-03
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/parallax-core42
keywords: [computational pathology, histology, H&E, batch effects, dataset quality control, interpretable features]
abstract: >
  A frozen, deterministic 42-axis patch-level measurement instrument for H&E images,
  reconstructed from the Parallax Pathology v4.1 kernel with 42/42 axes reproduced
  exactly. Intended for finding how a dataset was made (site, scanner, production
  route, preparation) with named measurements, and as an interpretable block next to
  colour features. Release engineering by Codex (OpenAI); public packaging and analysis
  with Claude (Anthropic).
